#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f67ffc2f-680d-5cc6-a154-58e08b1bea4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286329} {:answer/id #uuid "a77a25e4-1532-5fe5-96f8-d52197463720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286330} {:answer/id #uuid "c759e328-d237-5131-a459-dd2ac09738a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286331} {:answer/id #uuid "f9912763-e233-572c-9945-18af489f6217" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286332} {:answer/id #uuid "3ce4fa79-c313-53b3-ab65-6034ed4240f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f67ffc2f-680d-5cc6-a154-58e08b1bea4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286329} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fe145e9-45ba-50d5-9dc7-6044f32ba04b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "97e41006-c01d-55c0-bdd6-ad1a3b1505cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-102802" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y=4 \\\\ 6=5x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y=4 \\\\ 5x=6.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286334 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42ecbd60-a668-58ed-ac98-7410304eca2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286336} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd11ca0-6eaa-5b15-a9d8-3bebc70d407d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286337} {:answer/id #uuid "e930e7f0-e744-549f-a8ee-6f622366a32a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286338} {:answer/id #uuid "7cc88d4d-e3f8-5cad-82e8-4ff464eb4dc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286339} {:answer/id #uuid "6cc81260-a13c-5540-b089-64fde5b760e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cc88d4d-e3f8-5cad-82e8-4ff464eb4dc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286339} :answer-field/id #uuid "86dffe81-c5ea-5a48-80c9-5accf5c4f9ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "227f5432-14f9-5618-8402-19510df62a5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-12285" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x-4y=2 \\\\ -x+y=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 1-(-4)\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01681ac2-e161-567b-8a45-b934df1d456b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286343} {:answer/id #uuid "5121d015-f1d8-52bf-9d65-0cea17480a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5121d015-f1d8-52bf-9d65-0cea17480a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286344} :answer-field/id #uuid "32cde33b-9de2-5a38-ab81-1e07d7256b1a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286342} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cb5c507-528b-50a5-8985-9c5fa03c23e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cb5c507-528b-50a5-8985-9c5fa03c23e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286346} :answer-field/id #uuid "de5432b9-fedd-5640-9faf-47c1ca67c1e4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286345} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2808ac36-e8ac-5295-9c1f-d84ef7b7493c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2808ac36-e8ac-5295-9c1f-d84ef7b7493c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286348} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7f1347f-288e-5404-8433-c1128330b84b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a1ccae0e-0d02-5cab-8336-a50181fa21a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-320805" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=7 \\\\ 5x+2y=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-5$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $7$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-3$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-4$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-5$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-3$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286349 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5086b609-98bc-58bf-beb4-15826b65f735" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5086b609-98bc-58bf-beb4-15826b65f735" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286351} :answer-field/id #uuid "55c180ff-40cf-5e7b-99c4-b760bff5c38e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286350} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41e0f53e-3a49-557f-a1fd-251dd542d93a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41e0f53e-3a49-557f-a1fd-251dd542d93a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286353} :answer-field/id #uuid "b435363e-e168-5cea-b85f-766fd816101b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286352} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "795f3a2c-4192-5280-ad3b-987f1824abe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "795f3a2c-4192-5280-ad3b-987f1824abe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286355} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bd0fb3a-9a05-5e3a-bac6-78434b42f62c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "412a016b-e879-5727-b9bf-0c51b54f0a26" :question/math-academy-id "q-320836" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+8=0 \\\\ x=7+3y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $-3$ | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-1$ | {{field-2}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $7$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-3$ | $0$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+0y=-8 \\\\ x-3y=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286356 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50336411-1fa5-5ede-962e-0f9067f0173b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{50}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286358} {:answer/id #uuid "8e577c6e-12c2-5ac9-8f6c-342c5862f64e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 \\\\ -6 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286359} {:answer/id #uuid "dfb7f0bc-862e-5a37-9056-f59979467bb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{50}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286360} {:answer/id #uuid "15c7f7c9-a850-5b04-a269-df4f141633d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286361} {:answer/id #uuid "81201c97-fe44-565d-b701-3f21d12bd4ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81201c97-fe44-565d-b701-3f21d12bd4ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286362} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4d621bb-24d8-503d-8db5-4373766fe8dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "34c426c5-7657-5020-93fd-26e20c441212" :question/math-academy-id "q-32139" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+6y=46 \\\\ 8x+y=-23\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 1-6\\cdot 8}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
